    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, the Austin Waves offense is anchored by **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) and **Josh Lowe** (71.68), who present the most compelling profiles. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** leverages a prime spot in the two-hole against Young, benefiting significantly from a favorable matchup against a starter with a 4.77 xERA and a potent dynamic platoon advantage. Similarly, **Josh Lowe** is a priority start despite the lower lineup position; his massive 19% boost from the opposing SP skill level and the favorable wind conditions at the park make him a top-tier play to chase speed and counting stats. **Kyle Tucker** (71.10) remains a cornerstone of the outfield, maintaining high efficiency despite facing Rodriguez, bolstered by wind support and his high-floor base projection.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench today involves **Dominic Smith** (56.83) and **Coby Mayo** (56.80), both of whom were displaced by the depth of our middle-of-the-order production. **Dominic Smith** was the closest to cracking the starting nine, but he was ultimately relegated to the bench because his aggregate efficiency score, while respectable, could not displace the higher platoon-adjusted outputs of **Andy Pages** (62.01) and **Sam Antonacci** (61.39). While **Miguel Vargas** remains a specialized asset due to his 63% SB profile, he was excluded to prioritize raw run-production categories today.\n\nRisk management remains a priority given the volatility of the current lineup. **Jackson Merrill** (56.95) carries the most uncertainty, as his score is contingent on a \"Lineup Pending\" status; if he is not confirmed in the leadoff spot as assumed, his efficiency will likely dip further due to the tough matchup against Kirby. Meanwhile, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (60.74) faces a \"Wind In\" advisory that slightly tempers his power upside against Flaherty, though his xwOBA remains high enough to warrant the start. Managers should monitor the weather in his park closely as the afternoon progresses.",
